# golden-lock: keep these paths byte-for-byte stable across checkouts.
#
# The manifest records the SHA-256 of each locked file's exact bytes. If git's
# autocrlf rewrites line endings on checkout (LF<->CRLF), the bytes on disk no
# longer match what was hashed and `golden-lock verify` reports a spurious
# mismatch (exit 1). `-text` tells git to never translate EOLs for these paths,
# so the hashes stay valid on macOS, Linux, Windows, and WSL alike.

# The manifest itself — its parsing and the hashes it stores depend on exact
# bytes; a stray CR would corrupt a path or hash line. Slash-less pattern, so it
# matches golden.lock at any depth.
golden.lock             -text

# Convention from the /golden-test skill: extracted core tests are *.golden.*
# siblings (e.g. auth.golden.go, billing.golden.ts). Pin them all.
*.golden.*              -text

# Pin individual locked files explicitly as you lock them (uncomment + edit):
# internal/auth/auth_golden_test.go   -text
# tests/golden/**                     -text
